# Decisions

## Stack
Chose Python + scikit-learn TF-IDF for retrieval instead of an
embedding model (e.g. sentence-transformers) or a vector DB (Chroma).
Reason: zero setup dependencies, runs offline, installs in seconds,
and is enough to prove the core requirement (grounded, cited
answers with a refusal path) under a very tight build window.

## Rejected: embeddings / vector DB
Semantic embeddings (like the ChromaDB + LangGraph setup used in an
earlier local RAG project) would handle paraphrased questions much
better than TF-IDF keyword matching. Rejected for this build only
because of time — first priority was a working, honest floor, not
the strongest possible retrieval.

## Rejected: LLM-generated answers
The assistant returns the clause text directly rather than having an
LLM rephrase it. This is deliberate, not just a time-cut: returning
the source text verbatim is the safest way to guarantee the answer
never says something the manual doesn't. An LLM rephrasing step
would read more natural but adds a risk of it drifting from what the
clause actually says.

## Confidence threshold
Set to 0.20 after testing. At 0.15, an unrelated question ("free
birthday cake") false-matched a real clause with an accessibility
answer. Raised the threshold until clearly off-topic questions were
refused while real questions still matched correctly. This threshold
is tuned against one small synthetic manual — it has not been
validated against a larger, real manual and would likely need
retuning.

## What this does not do
- No semantic retrieval (see above) — will miss paraphrased or
  indirect questions that don't share keywords with the clause.
- No web interface. A CLI is an accepted format for this problem.
- No handling of questions that require combining multiple clauses
  (e.g. "if I'm late reporting AND my application is incomplete") —
  it retrieves a single best-matching clause only.
- No logging/analytics of what questions get refused, which would be
  the natural next step for spotting manual gaps.

## What I'd fix first with more time
Swap TF-IDF for a local embedding model so paraphrased questions
match correctly, and add multi-clause retrieval for compound
questions.